 "notes": [
  "The zero line carries nothing on these pairs. On 1h, CMF(20) crossing up through 0 gave 9,302 entries in 3,058 separate moves. Twenty candles later those entries were 0.01% ahead of random entries, well inside the luck band. The short on a cross down through 0 landed inside the band too: 0.03% on 1h, 0.23% on 4h and 0.72% on daily.",
  "On daily, entering long while CMF(20) was below −0.10 gave 784 entries in 73 moves. Twenty days later they were 7% behind random entries. The gap holds without its strongest stretch, between Apr 13 and Jun 14, 2022, and shows again at 50 candles. At 10 and 100 candles it was the same as random. On 1h and 4h the same setting was the same as random.",
  "That daily result splits by trend. Above the 200-day SMA it did 9% worse than random, but that rests on entries between Jan 4 and Jan 19, 2022, so it is fragile. Below the 200-day SMA it was the same as random. No single coin had enough separate moves to be judged on its own.",
  "CMF(20) above 0.05 on daily beat random by 3%, but 120 entries between Dec 28, 2020 and May 11, 2021 carry it. Without them it was the same as random, and it was also the same at 50 and 100 candles. In uptrends it looked 2% better, resting on the stretch between Sep 2, 2020 and Jan 2, 2022. In downtrends it was the same as random. On 1h this level holds about seven times as often as the cross up through 0, and it was still the same as random.",
  "Some splits by trend look like results but rest on a handful of entries. On daily in downtrends, the cross up through 0 beat random by 3%, and the short on the cross down did 3% worse than random. Each rests on 5 entries from one rebound: signals between Jun 10 and Jun 29, 2023 for the cross up, and between Jun 9 and Jun 28, 2023 for the cross down. On 4h in downtrends, CMF(20) below −0.10 beat random by 0.64%, but only because of signals between Dec 28, 2022 and Jan 2, 2023.",
  "For a long DCA bot, CMF zero crosses do not time entries on these pairs, so the take profit and DCA orders do the work. On daily, CMF(20) below −0.10 marked selling that kept going. Treat it as a reason to leave a dip-buying start condition off, not as a trigger. CMF(20) above 0.05 on daily is at most a trend filter to test beside your other conditions."
